.TH CRAFT 6 "November 2026" "craft 3.5.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
craft \- CRAFT: The Vicious Vikings, a real-time strategy game for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B craft
.RB [ \-scale
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-record
.IR FILE " |"
.B \-\-replay
.IR FILE
.RB [ \-\-no\-view ]]
.RB [ \-\-host ]
.RB [ \-\-join
.I HOST
.B \-\-code
.I CODE
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B craft
is a real-time strategy game in the style of Warcraft and Dune II.
As a Viking king, you build up a settlement, feed up to 70 citizens,
harvest gold and wood, trade, and train knights, archers, catapults and
ships to conquer the computer players' islands.
.PP
A start menu lets you choose the world (with or without islands,
local sight, a king unit, random seed), the human and computer players,
and their settings.
Press
.B Play
to start.
.PP
Press
.B save
during a game to save it, and
.B restore
in the start menu to continue a saved game.
.PP
On large screens the game is zoomed (1.25\(mu, 1.5\(mu, 2\(mu or 3\(mu).
By default the largest step that fits the screen is used; change it
with the zoom buttons on the start menu's
.B Details
page.
.PP
Sound effects and music play through PipeWire, PulseAudio or ALSA.
Music volume and effects volume are on the start menu's
.B Details
page;
.B Shift+M
mutes or unmutes during a game. Music files (Ogg, MP3, FLAC or WAV)
go in
.IR ~/.local/share/craft/music :
.I menu.*
plays on the start menu,
.I win.*
and
.I lose.*
at the end of a game, and the rest are shuffled during play.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-scale " N"
Zoom the game
.I N
times (1 to 4, for example 1.5) for this run only, instead of the zoom
set in the start menu.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " FILE"
Record the game to
.IR FILE .
Without this option every game is recorded to
.IR ~/.local/share/craft/replays/last.craftreplay ,
which the next game replaces.
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " FILE"
Play a recorded game back. The orders come from the recording, not from
the mouse. Along the way the game checks that it plays out exactly as it
did when recorded, and at the end it prints
.B matched
or
.B DIVERGED
with the number of steps and a hash of the final state, and exits with
status 0 (matched) or 3 (diverged). Combine with
.B CRAFT_PROFILE=fast
to play the recording back as fast as possible.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-view
With
.BR \-\-replay :
play the recording back without opening any window (no X display is
needed), as fast as possible.
.TP
.B \-\-host
Host a network game. Every person seat on the start menu after your own
is played by a guest; after
.B Play
the game waits for them and prints a join code.
.TP
.BI \-\-join " HOST"
Join the game hosted at
.I HOST
(or
.IR HOST:PORT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-code " CODE"
The join code the host was given.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Your name in a network game (default: your login name).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
The port to host on or join (default 47800). The host listens on
127.0.0.1 only; guests on other computers reach it through SSH.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X display to use.
.TP
.B CRAFT_DATADIR
Directory that holds the game data
.RI ( hcraft/ ,
.IR buttons/ " and"
.IR .windefaults.params ).
If unset,
.B craft
uses the current directory when it holds the data, and otherwise the
installed data directory.
.TP
.B CRAFT_SOUND
Set to
.B off
to play without sound.
.TP
.B CRAFT_SOUND_DEBUG
If set, log every sound effect to standard error, with whether it was
played.
.TP
.B CRAFT_SOUND_RECORD
Write the game's sound to this WAV file instead of playing it (for
testing).
.TP
.B CRAFT_PROFILE
If set, print step timings to standard error every 200 steps.
The value
.B fast
also runs the game as fast as it can, for testing.
.TP
.B CRAFT_REPLAY
Set to
.B off
to stop recording games to
.IR last.craftreplay .
.TP
.B CRAFT_REPLAY_DUMP
A directory. At every check (each 200 steps) the game writes a readable
breakdown of its state there, as
.IR rec-STEP.txt
while recording and
.IR play-STEP.txt
while playing back, so a diverging replay can be tracked down with
.BR diff (1).
.TP
.B CRAFT_REPLAY_VERBOSE
If set, print each check that matched during playback.
.TP
.B CRAFT_SEED
Use this number to make the map of a new game instead of the one the
start menu chose, to make the same map again (each new game prints its
seed).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Replays are kept in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/craft/replays .
Saved games are kept in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/craft/saves ,
by default
.IR ~/.local/share/craft/saves .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The zoom setting is kept in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/craft/settings ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/craft/settings .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/craft/
Installed pictures, button icons and window defaults.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/doc/craft/html/craft.html
The original game manual: units, buildings and orders.
.SH SEE ALSO
The art tools
.BR craft\-cmedit ,
.BR craft\-ppm2cmap ,
.BR craft\-mirror ,
.BR craft\-split ,
.BR craft\-recolor ,
.BR craft\-shade ,
.BR craft\-medit ,
.BR craft\-morph " and"
.BR craft\-compress
are described in README.md.
